- Metric
    Architect
        - scope of what must be done
            target: full content derived to most useful level with sharp boundaries
            actual: incomplete operational understanding baised to specific viewpoint
            measurement operation used: rank
            grade interval minimum: f
            grade interval maximum: a
            is minimum ranking open: yes
            is maximum ranking open: yes
            number of grades: 6
        - natural functional decomposition
            target: higher order types are better
            actual: unnatural functional decomposition with low cohesion and high coupling
        - shared understanding
            target: understanding between reader and writer
            actual: contention or malfunction of functional understanding
            - peer objective cohesion
                target: peer child objective follows "magic formula" in sequence to achieve parent objective
                actual: unclear or ambiguous functions defined
            - terminology defined
                target: specific reader terms integrated into standardised industry terminology
                actual: different understanding of function between reader and writer

    Reader
        - essential elements evaluation against motivation
        - identify outputs required
        - intrinsic dependencies
            

- Workflow
    Facilitator                    |after facilitator
    determine system objective     |
    derive motivation              |determine system objective
    evaluate business process      |derive motivation
    prioritised functional delivery|evaluate business process

    

        
- Graph
    
    Function
        parent function
        is external: no
        criticality: importance to achieve parent function
        business priority

        Objective (Result)
            term format: verb + qualified object
            frequency: how often the result is needed to achieve parent function

        Type
    Attribute
        function
        Input
        Output
        Descriptive
    Rule
        Objective Rule 
            - Naming
                - transitive verb + qualified object → `Calculate Payment`. One verb per objective, named objectively.
                - Forbidden
                    - Vague service verbs: "manage", "ensure"
                    - Performance terms: "good", "acceptable"
                    - Information-management words: "information", "data", "content", "info"
                    - Political words: "Business", "IT", "Management", "Support", "Execution"
                    - Flow words: "then", "next"
            - Decomposition rules
                - 3 to 7 sub-objectives per parent objective.
                - Test each split
                    - Ask Why: Every subresult's reason is the parent
                    - Ask How: All subresults together must achieve parent
                - Attributes may be attached to objectives to describe their arguments and results.
                    - Parent and child IO
                    - Descriptive attributes added
            - General Objectives
                - First Thing And Last Thing Works Well With Parent
                - Sequence Of Peers Follows "Magic Formula" For Cohesion
            - Remove Non-Functional Coupling
                - Location
                - Procedural
                - Data
            - Generalise Similar Methods Of Different Parent Objectives
            - Regroup Results Used Multiple Times as Peers
            - Only Execution Allowed (no planning)
        Type Rule
            - Specific Natural Typing
                - Ask Which: Define of the highest possible parent
                - Mutually Exclusive
                - Completeness testing
    Session
        - Problem Solving
        - Design
- Function

    Determine Measurement
        - Effect
        - Control
    Formulate Objective
    Link To Parent Function
    Reorganise Function Tree
        input rule
        output architect
    Discover Entity
        - Input
        - Output
        - Qualified Object
    Map Function Timing
        importance
        frequency

       


- Example
    Do Value Chain Activity
        - Primary
            Promote brand offering (Marketing & Sales)
                - Launch social media ad campaigns
                - Negotiate vendor contracts with retail partners
                - Publish promotional discounts for seasonal sales
            Manage inbound material (Inbound Logistics)
                - Unload raw steel from delivery trucks
                - Inspect organic ingredients for quality assurance
                - Store digital components in temperature-controlled warehouses
            Transform raw input (Operations)
                - Assemble electronic circuits on the production line
                - Bake artisan bread in commercial ovens
                - Package finished apparel into retail-ready boxes
            Distribute finished product (Outbound Logistics)
                - Load delivery fleets for regional distribution
                - Fulfill online orders via third-party couriers
                - Dispatch bulk cargo to international shipping ports
            Support final customer (Service)
                - Repair broken hardware under warranty agreements
                - Process product returns via customer service
                - Troubleshoot software glitches over live chat
        - Support
            Govern company infrastructure (Firm Infrastructure)
                - Audit financial ledgers
                - Draft legal contracts
                - Secure internal networks (Against cyber threats)
            Develop human talent (Human Resource Management)
                - Interview engineering candidates
                - Conduct safety training
                - Administer employee benefits
                    - payroll systems
                    - ...
                - payroll systems
                - ...
            Advance proprietary technology (Technological Development)
                - Code automated features
                - Test alternative materials
                - Upgrade database servers
            Source essential good (Procurement)
                - Source raw fabrics
                - Purchase office equipment
                - Approve vendor bids